    VALUES (v_bag, v_section, $q$Carl's HotShot Golf Mat System$q$, $q$Carl's Place$q$, $q$the builder who wants to change the feel later without buying another mat, and anyone already buying a Carl's enclosure$q$, $q$It is the mat you can tune. Builders buy the standard, discover they want softer or firmer, and swap a $230 insert instead of a $1,000 mat. The YouTube reviews are mostly about which insert, not whether.$q$, $q$Pros: three swappable inserts: foam for joints, gel for realism, standard for real tees; Golfer Geeks 2026 Editor's Pick; Friendly Golfer calls the gel the best-feeling mat he has used; cheapest of the premium mats at $499.95 for a 4 x 5; ships rolled, so it is the easiest premium mat to store or move
Cons: base is extra and nearly doubles the cost (Golfer Geeks); foam and gel inserts do not take a real tee; many owners switch to cone tees; standard insert's three tee holes swallow balls on irons; slides on smooth floors without the base
